    The Silent Annex: first playable version
    
    An original third-person survival-horror game for desktop browsers,
    built with TypeScript, Three.js, Rapier and Vite, with no game engine.
    
    - 18 connected spaces across a reception wing, research wing and Level C
    - Three main puzzles plus two code locks, and two endings
    - The Hush: a stealth threat driven by player noise, with no combat
    - Inventory, journal with map, versioned saves with recovery, settings
    - Every texture, model and sound generated in code
    - 71 Vitest tests, including full playthroughs and a no-softlock solver
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
